          <sourceConnection xsi:type="archimate:Connection" id="id-071959a43ba443c7bdae9feca05d53e7" source="id-910dbc5264014b81a5d97d0ba2db4b2e" target="id-4eca995c002f41e681359e5e0aec4476" archimateRelationship="id-3dfbe94b114147e2a07ed5daa1aab311"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-dc96bc39a4564c48ac9175dfc6a6cb7b" targetConnections="id-5aac4adc8e4b44198c893cdf7db7d714" textPosition="1" archimateElement="id-53c6d3a2ddf84087bb2f6e66e5ab0334">
          <bounds x="408" y="264" width="120" height="55"/>
        </child>
        <documentation>Reasinon mode  is a classification axis that gates whether an **agent-intent**'s work is subject to the content-governance model — the combination of **Source-regime**, **Synthesis-regime**, and **Task Mode** — based on one question: does this step require an LLM to reason at all.&#xD;
&#xD;
**Leading question:** Does this agent-intent require an LLM to reason about meaning, or does it execute by fixed procedure with no reasoning?&#xD;
&#xD;
**Provenance**: replaces the retired **Mode of operation** concept (see Appendix — Deprecated terms). Mode of operation's three positions (Content, Representation-transforming, Conditional) answered three loosely related questions under one label; Determinism asks exactly one, and collapses the two non-content positions — both of which were, on inspection, already mechanical/rule-based rather than meaning-blind-with-exceptions — into a single **Deterministic** position. See `temp/claude-code-plans/plan-execution-nature.md` for the full migration record.&#xD;
&#xD;
### Characteristics ⭐&#xD;
- One of two **agent-intent** classification axes (alongside **Development phase**, which is agent-level — see Development phase, Explanation)&#xD;
- Is a **gate**, not a scale: each position determines *whether* Source-regime/Synthesis-regime/Task Mode apply, not *how much* meaning-transformation is permitted&#xD;
- Independent of other axes, including **Execution Strategy**: Execution Strategy governs how a *sequence* of steps progresses and has no vocabulary for whether one step is mechanical; Determinism governs whether one step requires reasoning at all and has no vocabulary for sequencing. A single Orchestration Specification may freely compose Deterministic and Cognitive steps under any Execution Strategy — neither axis may be inferred from, or used to infer, the other (see Execution Strategy, Relationships)&#xD;
- A **Deterministic** agent-intent is realised as a script, never as an LLM call; a **Cognitive** agent-intent is realised as an LLM call with full content-governance applying&#xD;
&#xD;
### What it is not ❌&#xD;
- Not a meaning-transformation scale (that is **Synthesis-regime**)&#xD;
- Not a task-shape classification (that is **Task Mode**)&#xD;
- Not a progression-logic constraint (that is **Execution Strategy**) — see Characteristics&#xD;
- Not redundant with Synthesis-regime or Task Mode: its positions gate whether those two axes (and Source-regime) apply, they do not duplicate a value on either axis's scale&#xD;
&#xD;
### Synonyms 🏷️&#xD;
- Cognitive gate&#xD;
&#xD;
### Explanation 💬&#xD;
Reasoning mode distinguishes agent-intents that require an LLM to reason from work that is realised as a script and never invokes an LLM at all — mechanical representation-conversion and rule-based condition/hygiene checks alike. Because a Deterministic step never invokes an LLM, it never has content to govern and never has a temperature to calibrate (see `foundations/.canonical/data-model/logical-seed/seed.model.md` §7, collapsed to the Cognitive dimension only as part of this migration).&#xD;
&#xD;
**Binding level**: bound to **agent-intent**, matching Mode of operation's corrected binding level (not Agent) — declared per intent, alongside Source-regime, Synthesis-regime, and Task Mode where those apply.&#xD;
&#xD;
### Positions (Position Elements) 📋&#xD;
&#xD;
| Position | Element classification | Description | Content-governance model applies? |&#xD;
|---|---|---|---|&#xD;
| **Cognitive** | Position Element | Requires an LLM to reason about supplied material | Yes — Source-regime, Synthesis-regime, and Task Mode all apply and MUST be declared |&#xD;
| **Deterministic** | Position Element | Executes by fixed procedure with zero reasoning; realised as a script, never an LLM call | No — not applicable; a script has no Source-regime, Synthesis-regime, or Task Mode to declare, for the same reason it is not an agent-intent in the reasoning sense |&#xD;
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="components-and-services" id="id-4eeb3931b57c4fffa5d5f3ec1b9b6280">
